From afd2c8d7fbdd2fe81244cb8c65f542ffa58f6885 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [zigbee] Add OTA updates over Zigbee (ota platform: zigbee)

Adds the ZCL OTA Upgrade client cluster (0x0019) to an endpoint so that
Zigbee2MQTT or ZHA can update the firmware over the Zigbee network.

- zigbee: listener hook in the existing action handler, so the OTA
  callbacks reach the OTA platform without replacing the handler
  (attribute writes for number/switch keep working)
- zigbee/ota: ota platform built on the ESP-IDF OTA backend (rollback
  and safe_mode work as for the other OTA platforms); unpacks a raw or
  zlib-compressed image from the OTA file; on_begin/on_progress/on_end/
  on_error triggers
- the build writes firmware.zigbee.ota next to firmware.ota.bin, and the
  dashboard offers it as a download

File parsing, block resync and stall handling adapted from
github.com/jabla/esphome-hiflow-zigbee (MIT).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TAigdDwPTsH7gxNNraUrHU
